        "original_id": "8f5ce8b8-5f0b-5b6c-8b8c-7795da6115bd",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Abraham Lincoln Neiman, Carrie Marcus Neiman, Herbert Marcus, Minnie Lichtenstein Marcus\n- Companies: A. Harris & Company, Neiman Marcus\n- Places: Chicago, Illinois; Cleveland, Ohio; Dallas, Texas; Atlanta, Georgia\n- Topics: marriage, retail business founding, sales promotion work\n\nFacts:\n- Abraham Lincoln Neiman was born on July 4, 1875, in Chicago, Illinois, and he was raised in a Jewish orphanage in Cleveland, Ohio.\n- Carrie Marcus Neiman was born on May 3, 1883, and she later became an American businessperson and a cofounder of Neiman Marcus, a luxury department store.\n- Abraham Lincoln Neiman met Carrie Marcus Neiman in Dallas, Texas, while both were working at A. Harris & Company.\n- Abraham Lincoln Neiman and Carrie Marcus Neiman married in 1905 and moved to Atlanta, Georgia, with Herbert Marcus and Minnie Lichtenstein Marcus to do sales promotion work.\n- The Neiman and Marcus families relinquished rights to sales territories in a nascent soft drink concern for $25,000, and they used that money to open Neiman Marcus in Dallas in 1907.\n- Carrie Marcus Neiman died on March 6, 1953.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
